#DESCRIPTION
Inflow / outflow open-boundary regression test for the hybrid solver:
a uniform magnetized plasma streams along +x through a 1D domain with
inflow at -x and outflow at +x.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
F                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#FIELDBOXBOUNDARY
inflow                  fieldBoxBoundaryLo
outflow                 fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi

#PARTICLEBOXBOUNDARY
0                       iSpecies
inflow                  particleBoxBoundaryLo
outflow                 particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#HALLTERM
F                       useHallTerm

#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

#INFLOW
5.0                      rho [amu/cc]
20.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                      uy [km/s]
0.0                      uz [km/s]
10000.0                  T [K]

#BSUBCYCLE
1                       nBSubcycle

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
20.0                    ux [km/s]      uniform bulk flow along +x (U_code = 0.2)
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
1.0439e-8               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = 1 s; sets cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
10.0                    dt
1                       dx

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
10.0                    TimeMax   ~1.6 ion gyroperiods (stability)

#RUN
